  "question": {
    "text": "At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>K</mi></math>, the rms speed of oxygen molecules is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mi>&#945;</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math>&nbsp;times to that of its average speed in the&nbsp;gas. Then, the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> will be (use&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>22</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math>)"
  },
